{
  "enabled": false,
  "name": "Update README on Power Changes",
  "description": "DISABLED by choice. Would update README.md when POWER.md, mcp.json or steering files change. Two problems fixed if it is ever re-enabled: README.md removed from the trigger patterns (it used to rewrite the file that triggers it, so it retriggered itself indefinitely), and the prompt now refuses to act on files outside this workspace, because the patterns match on filename and fire for same-named files anywhere on disk.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "POWER.md",
      "mcp.json",
      "steering/*.md",
      "steering/**/*.md"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A power definition file may have been edited. Before doing anything, run these scope checks against the JSON payload you were given.\n\nCHECK 1 - IN WORKSPACE. The payload contains `cwd` (the workspace root) and `file_path` (the saved file). If `file_path` does not begin with `cwd`, the hook has fired on an unrelated file that merely shares a filename. These patterns match on filename and are NOT anchored to the workspace. STOP. Change nothing. Reply in one line that the hook fired out of scope on <file_path> and no action was taken.\n\nCHECK 2 - IS A POWER DEFINITION FILE. Compute the path of `file_path` relative to `cwd`. Proceed ONLY if that relative path is exactly `POWER.md` or `mcp.json`, or matches `steering/*.md` or `steering/**/*.md`. If it is `README.md`, STOP - this hook must never be triggered by the file it edits. If the relative path starts with `deploy/`, STOP - that is generated output, not source.\n\nONLY IF THE CHECKS PASS: review what actually changed in that file and update `README.md` at the workspace root to reflect any new or modified features, capabilities, MCP server configuration or prerequisites. Keep it concise and user-facing: what the power does, key features, prerequisites, how to use it.\n\nPRESERVE THESE - they are deliberate and must survive any regeneration:\n- The Supported Modernization Paths table: 7 numbered rows across 6 source families, with the .NET-to-Java row marked BETA, plus the Cross-Cutting Dimensions table beneath it\n- The note that no \".NET 8 first, then Java\" bridge pathway is ever proposed\n- The Output section listing exactly 11 report sections, matching steering/report-structure.md. Do not renumber it and do not add a 12th\n- The statement that all 13 steering files are inclusion: manual and reachable from the POWER.md dispatch table\n- The Version History entries\n\nMake the smallest edit that reflects the change. Do not rewrite sections that did not change, and do not paraphrase the items listed above."
  }
}
